# Minutes of a housing co-operative's general meeting, on US Letter paper, written almost entirely in Markdown: the
# body is one Markdown with numbered headings (Numbered in the rules of Heading 2 and Heading 3), nested bulleted and
# numbered lists with their own markers per level (Bullet markers, Number markers), two GFM tables with aligned
# columns, a block quote, a horizontal rule and, inline, bold, italic, ++underline++, ~~strikethrough~~ (an item
# withdrawn from the agenda), `code` and links. The engine styles the block quote and the rule with the For element
# rules of Block quote and Divider. Two footnotes are called from the Markdown ([^id]). The meeting details are a
# Grid of labels and values above it, the signatures a Stack kept together, and the first page carries a "Draft"
# stamp, a Page overlay rotated 8 degrees that appears only there (Pages: first).
